The following is a list of squads for each nation competing at [[UEFA Euro 2008]] in Austria and Switzerland. The tournament started on 7 June and the [[UEFA Euro 2008 final|final]] took place in [[Vienna]] on 29 June 2008.<ref>{{cite web |title=UEFA EURO 2008 squad lists announced |url=https://www.uefa.com/MultimediaFiles/Download/PressRelease/uefa/UEFAMedia/70/24/56/702456_DOWNLOAD.pdf|work=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=28 May 2008 |access-date=6 September 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120620184829/http://www.uefa.com/multimediafiles/download/pressrelease/uefa/uefamedia/70/24/56/702456_download.pdf |archive-date=20 June 2012 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Final squads announced for EURO |url=http://en.archive.uefa.com/news/kind=1/newsid=702209.html |work=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=28 May 2008 |access-date=6 September 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://archive.today/20130105013518/http://en.archive.uefa.com/news/kind=1/newsid=702209.html |archive-date=5 January 2013 }}</ref>

Each national team had to submit a squad of 23 players, three of whom had to be goalkeepers, by 28 May 2008. If a player was injured severely enough to prevent his participation in the tournament before his team's first match, he could be replaced by another player.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/MultimediaFiles/Download/PressConference/Competitions/MediaServices/68/13/42/681342_DOWNLOAD.pdf |title=Regulations of the UEFA European Football Championship 2006/08 |access-date=29 July 2014|publisher=UEFA |page=19 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140809112907/https://www.uefa.com/MultimediaFiles/Download/PressConference/Competitions/MediaServices/68/13/42/681342_DOWNLOAD.pdf |archive-date=9 August 2014 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

All caps, goals, ages, and clubs of players are correct as of 7 June 2008, the first day of the tournament.

